So ... we make "magical music" a skill.  A skill in which some classes
never go beyond "unskilled", a few can become "basic", and only a bard
can reach "expert" in.

We need to assign songs degrees of difficulty, perhaps, with a chance
of failure. The lower your skill and experience level, the lower your
chance of success and/or the effect generated.   Much as magic is
handled for wizards -- all classes can use magic, but only wizards can
cast "fireball" such that it sets off 8 explosions of fire.

